00:03:58.502 --> 00:04:01.046
And here's one way you
never better yourself:

00:04:01.046 --> 00:04:03.194
when you come up with excuses for why

00:04:03.194 --> 00:04:05.075
other people are
successful, and you're not.

00:04:05.075 --> 00:04:07.444
That (bleep) is (bleeping) dangerous.

00:04:07.444 --> 00:04:08.972
When you give yourself an escape.

00:04:08.972 --> 00:04:11.915
Yeah, well that's easy for you to say,

00:04:11.915 --> 00:04:12.748
You know, you do this...

00:04:12.748 --> 00:04:13.610
Trust me.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:15.311
Everybody has a hard road.

00:04:15.311 --> 00:04:17.407
I wanted to jump out
a window several times

00:04:17.407 --> 00:04:18.948
during my young life.

00:04:18.948 --> 00:04:20.968
I wanted to jump in front
of a (bleeping) train,

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:22.896
just end it because
it's too much pressure.

00:04:22.896 --> 00:04:23.813
Not really.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.589
But you know what I'm
saying, theoretically.

00:04:26.589 --> 00:04:27.916
We all go through hard times,

00:04:27.916 --> 00:04:29.109
we all go through depression,

00:04:29.109 --> 00:04:32.212
we all go through doubt
and moments in your life

00:04:32.212 --> 00:04:35.124
when it's really (bleeping) difficult

00:04:35.124 --> 00:04:37.003
and you're trying to
figure out what the (bleep)

00:04:37.003 --> 00:04:37.993
your path is going to be.

00:04:37.993 --> 00:04:39.363
It's hard as (bleep).

00:04:39.363 --> 00:04:41.215
But Steph and I were talking about this

00:04:41.215 --> 00:04:42.641
before this podcast starts,

00:04:42.641 --> 00:04:45.120
that that is what makes you a person.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.488
And those difficult moments
are what build your character

00:04:47.488 --> 00:04:51.839
Show me a great man who's
the son of a great man,

00:04:51.839 --> 00:04:52.896
that's what we're saying.

00:04:52.896 --> 00:04:54.053
You know, these kids that were

00:04:54.053 --> 00:04:56.652
born billionaires, you're (bleeped).

00:04:56.652 --> 00:04:57.485
You're (bleeped).

00:04:57.485 --> 00:05:00.617
You're never going to
be a self-made person.

00:05:00.617 --> 00:05:03.517
You have a back-up trust
for your back-up trust

00:05:03.517 --> 00:05:06.862
for your trust, and you're (bleeped), man.

00:05:06.862 --> 00:05:08.994
- By experiencing pain in your muscles

00:05:08.994 --> 00:05:13.031
and aching, then go on
and go on and go on,

00:05:13.031 --> 00:05:15.474
and those last two or
three or four repetitions,

00:05:15.474 --> 00:05:17.759
that's what makes actually
the muscle then grow.

00:05:17.759 --> 00:05:20.403
And that divides one
from being a champion,

00:05:20.403 --> 00:05:22.295
and one from not being a champion.

00:05:22.295 --> 00:05:24.439
If you can go through this pain period,

00:05:24.439 --> 00:05:26.229
you may get to be a champion.

00:05:26.229 --> 00:05:27.471
If you can't get through, forget it.

00:05:27.471 --> 00:05:29.442
And that's what most people lack,

00:05:29.442 --> 00:05:31.025
is having the guts.

00:05:32.243 --> 00:05:34.550
The guts to go in, and go through,

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.593
and say, I don't care what happens.

00:05:36.593 --> 00:05:38.281
It aches, and if I fall down...

00:05:38.281 --> 00:05:40.661
I have no fear of fainting in a gym,

00:05:40.661 --> 00:05:42.973
because I know it could happen,

00:05:42.973 --> 00:05:45.618
I threw up many times
while I was working out,

00:05:45.618 --> 00:05:47.301
but it doesn't matter.

00:05:47.301 --> 00:05:48.999
Because it's all worth it.

00:05:48.999 --> 00:05:50.452
- I wasn't happy,

00:05:50.452 --> 00:05:52.728
focused on the short term money coming in

00:05:52.728 --> 00:05:53.917
when creating a company,

00:05:53.917 --> 00:05:56.340
because otherwise the company will die.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:57.173
So the...

00:05:58.246 --> 00:06:01.291
A lot of times people think,

00:06:01.291 --> 00:06:03.860
creating a company is going to be fun.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:06.145
It's really not that fun.

00:06:06.145 --> 00:06:07.843
I mean, there are periods of fun.

00:06:07.843 --> 00:06:11.795
And there are periods
where it's just awful.

00:06:11.795 --> 00:06:15.017
And particularly, if you're
the CEO of a company,

00:06:15.017 --> 00:06:16.698
you actually a have distillation
of all the worst problems

00:06:16.698 --> 00:06:17.948
in the company.

00:06:19.866 --> 00:06:21.308
There's no point in spending your time

00:06:21.308 --> 00:06:23.736
on things that are going right,

00:06:23.736 --> 00:06:24.998
so you're only spending
your time on things

00:06:24.998 --> 00:06:26.821
that are going wrong.

00:06:26.821 --> 00:06:28.207
And there are things that are going wrong

00:06:28.207 --> 00:06:30.370
that other people can't take care of.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:31.849
So you're the worst...

00:06:31.849 --> 00:06:33.615
You have a filter for
the crappiest problem

00:06:33.615 --> 00:06:35.256
in the company.

00:06:35.256 --> 00:06:38.589
The most pernicious and painful problem.

00:06:39.761 --> 00:06:41.196
I wouldn't say it's...

00:06:41.196 --> 00:06:45.739
I think you have to feel
quite compelled to do it,

00:06:45.739 --> 00:06:47.586
and have a fairly high pain threshold.

00:06:47.586 --> 00:06:49.457
And there's a friend of mine who says,

00:06:49.457 --> 00:06:51.690
starting a company is like
staring into the abyss,

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:53.802
and eating glass.

00:06:53.802 --> 00:06:56.385
And there's some truth to that.

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.466
The staring into the abyss part

00:07:00.466 --> 00:07:04.136
is that you're going
to be constantly facing

00:07:04.136 --> 00:07:05.844
the extermination of the company.

00:07:05.844 --> 00:07:08.363
Because most start-ups fail.

00:07:08.363 --> 00:07:12.418
It's like 90%, 99% of start-ups fail.

00:07:12.418 --> 00:07:16.112
So that's the staring into the abyss part,

00:07:16.112 --> 00:07:17.707
you're constantly saying, okay,

00:07:17.707 --> 00:07:22.341
if I don't get this right,
the company will die.

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:25.576
Which can be quite stressful.

00:07:25.576 --> 00:07:28.775
And then, the eating glass part is,

00:07:28.775 --> 00:07:32.131
is you got to work on the problems

00:07:32.131 --> 00:07:34.723
the company needs you to work on,

00:07:34.723 --> 00:07:37.021
not the problems you want to work on.

00:07:37.021 --> 00:07:38.354
And so that's...

00:07:39.384 --> 00:07:40.900
You're going to wind
up working on problems

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:44.096
you really wish you weren't working on.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:46.284
And so that's the eating glass part.

00:07:46.284 --> 00:07:49.038
And so that goes on for a long time

00:07:49.038 --> 00:07:50.543
- [Audience Member] So
how do you keep your focus

00:07:50.543 --> 00:07:53.747
on the big picture when
you're constantly faced with,

00:07:53.747 --> 00:07:56.997
we could be out of business in a month.

00:07:58.598 --> 00:08:01.329
- Well, it's just a very small
percentage of mental energy

00:08:01.329 --> 00:08:03.049
is on the bigger picture.

00:08:03.049 --> 00:08:06.632
You know where you're
generally headed for,

00:08:07.496 --> 00:08:08.810
and the actual path is going to be

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:12.871
some sort of zig-zaggy
thing in that direction.

00:08:12.871 --> 00:08:15.363
You try not to deviate
too far from the path

00:08:15.363 --> 00:08:17.010
that you want to be on.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:21.578
But you're going to have
to do that to some degree.

00:08:21.578 --> 00:08:23.522
I don't want to diminish the...

00:08:23.522 --> 00:08:26.722
The profit motive is a good one,

00:08:26.722 --> 00:08:29.430
if the rules of an industry
are properly set up.

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:31.014
So there's nothing
fundamentally wrong with profit.

00:08:31.014 --> 00:08:34.626
In fact, profit just means
that people are paying you more

00:08:34.626 --> 00:08:36.435
for whatever you're doing,

00:08:36.435 --> 00:08:39.175
than you're spending to create.

00:08:39.175 --> 00:08:41.151
That's a good thing.

00:08:41.151 --> 00:08:43.990
And if that's not the case,

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.721
then you'll be out of
business and rightfully so.

00:08:47.721 --> 00:08:49.762
You're not adding enough value.

00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:53.828
- The key is what we do
in our times of pain.

00:08:53.828 --> 00:08:55.680
Pain will change us.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.616
Heartache, loss, disappointment,

00:08:57.616 --> 00:08:59.806
they don't leave us the same.

00:08:59.806 --> 00:09:01.558
When I lost my father,

00:09:01.558 --> 00:09:03.342
I didn't come out like I was before.

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:05.199
I was changed.

00:09:05.199 --> 00:09:08.133
If you go through a
divorce, a legal battle,

00:09:08.133 --> 00:09:09.651
a friend betrays you,

00:09:09.651 --> 00:09:12.173
eventually that will pass.

00:09:12.173 --> 00:09:15.763
You'll get through it,
but you'll be different.

00:09:15.763 --> 00:09:19.896
No how the pain changes you, is up to you.

00:09:19.896 --> 00:09:23.776
You can come out bitter,
or you can come out better.

00:09:23.776 --> 00:09:26.818
You can come out with a chip
on your shoulder, blaming God,

00:09:26.818 --> 00:09:28.880
or you can come out stronger,

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.234
with a greater confidence in God.

00:09:31.234 --> 00:09:34.764
You can come out defeated,
giving up on your dreams,

00:09:34.764 --> 00:09:37.980
or you can come out with
a new passion, a new fire,

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:41.201
excited about the new
opportunities in front of you.

00:09:41.201 --> 00:09:43.650
All of us experience pain.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:48.538
My challenge: don't just go
through it, grow through it.

00:09:48.538 --> 00:09:52.299
That difficulty is an
opportunity to get stronger,

00:09:52.299 --> 00:09:55.875
to develop character,
to gain new confidence.

00:09:55.875 --> 00:09:57.642
Anybody can give up,

00:09:57.642 --> 00:09:59.592
anybody can let it overwhelm you.

00:09:59.592 --> 00:10:01.264
But you know what that's doing?

00:10:01.264 --> 00:10:03.444
Wasting your pain.

00:10:03.444 --> 00:10:05.532
That pain is not there to stop you,

00:10:05.532 --> 00:10:06.770
it's there to prepare you,

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:09.783
to increase you, to develop you.

00:10:09.783 --> 00:10:11.379
- People used to take my
raps and crunch them up,

00:10:11.379 --> 00:10:13.229
and throw them on the ground.

00:10:13.229 --> 00:10:14.637
I used to get make fun of all the time,

00:10:14.637 --> 00:10:16.814
cause who believes that
the guy sitting next

00:10:16.814 --> 00:10:18.181
to them in math class is going

00:10:18.181 --> 00:10:19.369
to blow up and become a superstar?

00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:21.000
Right, you don't believe that.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.408
But like, you should have.

00:10:22.408 --> 00:10:23.876
And it's a bummer, you what I mean?

00:10:23.876 --> 00:10:26.177
Take it and make...

00:10:26.177 --> 00:10:29.111
You know, pain is the best inspiration.

00:10:29.111 --> 00:10:31.020
So if you're a creative out there

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:31.853
and you're getting bullied,

00:10:31.853 --> 00:10:33.836
take it and make
something great out of it.

00:10:33.836 --> 00:10:35.444
- Have you ever watched
the James Bond movie

00:10:35.444 --> 00:10:36.595
where it doesn't look like
he's losing at some point,

00:10:36.595 --> 00:10:37.859
and then he wins?

00:10:37.859 --> 00:10:38.692
Or Batman?

00:10:38.692 --> 00:10:39.525
Or Iron Man?

00:10:39.525 --> 00:10:40.358
Or any superhero?

00:10:40.358 --> 00:10:43.042
There has to be some diversity
for to overcome, to win.

00:10:43.042 --> 00:10:44.403
You can't be a champ unless you

00:10:44.403 --> 00:10:46.744
are in a place where you look
like you're going to lose,

00:10:46.744 --> 00:10:47.811
and then you win.

00:10:47.811 --> 00:10:49.708
The pain's that going to
come with being independent,

00:10:49.708 --> 00:10:50.824
you have to embrace it.

00:10:50.824 --> 00:10:52.049
Because it's going to happen.

00:10:52.049 --> 00:10:52.882
And also know that the
more successful you get,

00:10:52.882 --> 00:10:54.912
the more problems you're going to have,

00:10:54.912 --> 00:10:56.383
the more knots you're
going to have to untie.

00:10:56.383 --> 00:10:58.118
Being a boss does not mean smooth sailing,

00:10:58.118 --> 00:10:59.415
it means having the ability

00:10:59.415 --> 00:11:01.044
to care about other
people before yourself,

00:11:01.044 --> 00:11:03.180
and to untie problems, untie knots.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.335
That's all it is.

00:11:04.335 --> 00:11:06.530
It's not business if there's not problems.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.003
There's nothing good without struggle.

00:11:08.003 --> 00:11:09.034
It just doesn't happen.

00:11:09.034 --> 00:11:11.565
In all my experiences,
there hasn't been one thing

00:11:11.565 --> 00:11:13.059
that's been successful without me

00:11:13.059 --> 00:11:15.078
feeling some pain before
it was successful.

00:11:15.078 --> 00:11:17.164
So now when there is pain, I embrace it.

00:11:17.164 --> 00:11:18.631
I've been embracing it, I'm a G about it

00:11:18.631 --> 00:11:19.973
because I know that must mean,

00:11:19.973 --> 00:11:22.385
that if I'm cool, then, what awaits me...

00:11:22.385 --> 00:11:23.960
It's darkest before the dawn.

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:24.831
I don't want to sound corny,

00:11:24.831 --> 00:11:27.881
but that's what has to happen.

00:11:27.881 --> 00:11:29.435
- And I know that I personally

00:11:29.435 --> 00:11:31.818
that I personally have experienced

00:11:31.818 --> 00:11:32.749
quite a bit of disappointment in my life.

00:11:32.749 --> 00:11:35.219
And I'm assuming that you have as well.

00:11:35.219 --> 00:11:36.052
And guess what?

00:11:36.052 --> 00:11:38.260
We're going to continue to be disappointed

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:39.254
throughout our lives.

00:11:39.254 --> 00:11:40.375
At least we should be.

00:11:40.375 --> 00:11:41.377
Cause if you're not,

00:11:41.377 --> 00:11:43.674
that means that you're really not trying.

00:11:43.674 --> 00:11:46.030
Now how you handle yourself
post-disappointment,

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:49.602
this is critical to your
emotional and mental well-being.

00:11:49.602 --> 00:11:50.633
Pain.

00:11:50.633 --> 00:11:51.475
Pain.

00:11:51.475 --> 00:11:52.447
Hurtin'.

00:11:52.447 --> 00:11:53.280
Right?

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:54.434
It's part of the growing process.

00:11:54.434 --> 00:11:55.709
But I'll tell you something:

00:11:55.709 --> 00:11:58.096
life has a funny way of closing doors

00:11:58.096 --> 00:12:02.164
in order to keep you moving
in the right direction.

00:12:02.164 --> 00:12:04.291
So often in our society and as people,

00:12:04.291 --> 00:12:05.493
we run from pain.

00:12:05.493 --> 00:12:07.640
We do everything we can
to protect ourselves

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.536
and to shield ourselves
from feeling uncomfortable,

00:12:10.536 --> 00:12:11.968
that feeling of pain.

00:12:11.968 --> 00:12:13.666
And this is the reason why so many people

00:12:13.666 --> 00:12:16.352
abuse drugs, alcohol, casual sex.

00:12:16.352 --> 00:12:18.574
We do this to not feel the pain,

00:12:18.574 --> 00:12:20.335
but I'm saying, stop running.

00:12:20.335 --> 00:12:21.494
Stop trying to mask it.

00:12:21.494 --> 00:12:25.024
When you feel pain,
disappointment, it's okay.

00:12:25.024 --> 00:12:26.792
Don't try and cover it up.

00:12:26.792 --> 00:12:28.727
What you should do is actually embrace it.

00:12:28.727 --> 00:12:31.097
I know, it's easy for me sitting here,

00:12:31.097 --> 00:12:33.031
saying, oh, embrace the pain.

00:12:33.031 --> 00:12:35.160
You're feeling like crap,
don't worry about it.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:35.993
Feel it.

00:12:35.993 --> 00:12:37.082
Feel it.

00:12:37.082 --> 00:12:39.168
I get it, right, that's not...

00:12:39.168 --> 00:12:40.023
That's kind of a long shot.

00:12:40.023 --> 00:12:42.629
But what I'm saying, is
that the pain is normal,

00:12:42.629 --> 00:12:44.637
it's natural, it's a part
of the growth process.

00:12:44.637 --> 00:12:45.836
Learn from it.

00:12:45.836 --> 00:12:48.312
Once you do, you accept
it, you embrace it,

00:12:48.312 --> 00:12:49.886
learn from it, put it in its place,

00:12:49.886 --> 00:12:51.464
you're going to be able to move forward,

00:12:51.464 --> 00:12:53.530
faster, stronger, smarter.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.598
If you're not struggling
and getting disappointed

00:12:55.598 --> 00:12:58.069
from time to time, this probably means

00:12:58.069 --> 00:13:01.233
that you're not really
pushing your limits too far.

00:13:01.233 --> 00:13:02.201
All right, it's okay.

00:13:02.201 --> 00:13:06.166
Embrace it, don't get
discouraged, and stay focused.

00:13:06.166 --> 00:13:07.580
- Pain is a beautiful thing.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.378
Challenge is what life is about.

00:13:09.378 --> 00:13:12.411
A life without challenge,
a life without pain,

00:13:12.411 --> 00:13:14.330
is a life without growth.

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:15.192
And where is there no growth,

00:13:15.192 --> 00:13:17.859
there is stale, stagnant energy.

00:13:19.702 --> 00:13:20.965
And that's where most people live.

00:13:20.965 --> 00:13:24.168
Cause most people's
lives are designed around

00:13:24.168 --> 00:13:28.056
treading a path that is void of challenge.

00:13:28.056 --> 00:13:29.914
The minute they recognize
challenge or pain,

00:13:29.914 --> 00:13:31.678
they move away.

00:13:31.678 --> 00:13:32.872
This is a primal instinct,

00:13:32.872 --> 00:13:34.262
and normal and natural.

00:13:34.262 --> 00:13:36.567
But a weak perspective.

00:13:36.567 --> 00:13:38.800
Most people are bored, if you ask them.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:39.737
What do you think about your life.

00:13:39.737 --> 00:13:41.293
(sigh)

00:13:41.293 --> 00:13:43.576
Same old, same old.

00:13:43.576 --> 00:13:45.283
Every single day, what's the thing...

00:13:45.283 --> 00:13:48.052
Same (bleep), different day.

00:13:48.052 --> 00:13:49.346
Things of this nature.

00:13:49.346 --> 00:13:53.668
That's because they're
living their lives...

00:13:53.668 --> 00:13:54.585
in a lie...

00:13:56.023 --> 00:13:58.588
That is shrouded in comfort.

00:13:58.588 --> 00:14:00.327
It doesn't exist.

00:14:00.327 --> 00:14:01.465
They're not challenged,

00:14:01.465 --> 00:14:02.450
they're not growing.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:05.545
They're bored, and
they're better off dead.

00:14:05.545 --> 00:14:08.999
Your aliveness is found in your pain.

00:14:08.999 --> 00:14:12.978
Embrace it, love it, and grow from it.

00:14:12.978 --> 00:14:13.922
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:13.922 --> 00:14:15.240
I hope you enjoyed.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:17.083
I'd love to know, what did
you take from this video

00:14:17.083 --> 00:14:19.811
that you're going to
immediately apply somehow

00:14:19.811 --> 00:14:22.021
to your life, to your business.

00:14:22.021 --> 00:14:23.390
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:25.544
I'm really excited to
see what you have to say.

00:14:25.544 --> 00:14:26.832
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:14:26.832 --> 00:14:28.131
I believe in you,

00:14:28.131 --> 00:14:30.192
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:14:30.192 --> 00:14:32.515
and whatever your one word is.

00:14:32.515 --> 00:14:34.932
Much love, I'll see you soon.

